1
00:00:03,062 --> 00:00:07,428
(QExample) BOB: Hello, Pembroke Cycling Holidays, Bob speaking. Bob：

2
00:00:07,428 --> 00:00:09,113
MARGARET: Oh hello. Margaret：

3
00:00:09,113 --> 00:00:13,314
I've seen your advert for people to lead cycle trips.

4
00:00:13,314 --> 00:00:15,729
Are you the right person to speak to?

5
00:00:15,729 --> 00:00:17,955
BOB: Yes, I am. Bob：

6
00:00:17,955 --> 00:00:19,420
Could I have your name , please?

7
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:21,596
(Q1) MARGARET : It's Margaret Smith. Margaret：

8
00:00:21,596 --> 00:00:25,083
BOB: Are you looking for a permanent job, Margaret? Bob：Margaret，

9
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:33,109
[Q1答案句： temporary， 听出机会/听出方式： 场景词熟悉] MARGARET : No, temporary. I've got a permanent job starting in a few months' time, and I want to do something else until then.

10
00:00:33,109 --> 00:00:35,385
(Q2) [定位词work原词] BOB: What work do you do? Bob：

11
00:00:35,385 --> 00:00:44,320
[Q2答案句+Q2干扰： doctor， 时间干扰。 疑似选项： lawyer（无关信息+正确答案）] MARGARET : This will probably sound crazy - I used to be a lawyer, and then I made a complete career change and I'm going to be a doctor. Margaret：

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:46,571
I've just finished my training.

13
00:00:46,571 --> 00:00:48,053
BOB: Right. Bob：

14
00:00:48,053 --> 00:00:51,766
(Q3) [定位词： lead cycle] And have you had any experience of leading cycle trips?

15
00:00:51,766 --> 00:00:56,085
[Q3答案句： Africa] MARGARET : Yes, I've led several bike tours in Africa.&nbsp;

16
00:00:56,085 --> 00:01:06,815
[Q3干扰项： India， 下个月， cancel （正确答案+无关信息， 混合语义 cancel）] The trip to India that I had arranged to lead next month has now been cancelled, so when I saw you were advertising for tour leaders , I decided to apply.

17
00:01:06,815 --> 00:01:08,370
BOB: OK. Bob：

18
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:13,358
(Q4) Now we normally have two or three leaders on a trip, depending on the size of the group.

19
00:01:13,358 --> 00:01:23,687
Some tours are for very experienced cyclists , but we've got a tour coming up soon in Spain, which is proving so popular we need an additional leader.

20
00:01:23,687 --> 00:01:27,193
[跟定位] It's a cycling holiday for families. Would that suit you?

21
00:01:27,193 --> 00:01:29,142
MARGARET : It certainly would.&nbsp;

22
00:01:29,142 --> 00:01:36,814
I enjoy working with children, and I probably need some more experience before I go on a really challenging trip.

23
00:01:36,814 --> 00:01:42,215
BOB: That tour includes several teenagers : have you worked with that age group before?&nbsp;

24
00:01:42,215 --> 00:01:49,309
[Q4答案句：youth。      听出方式： 跟定位+同义替换  volunteer= voluntary，] MARGARET : Yes, I'm a volunteer worker in a youth club, where I help people to improve their cycling skills.&nbsp;

25
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:53,757
Before that I helped out in a cycling club where I taught beginners.

26
00:01:53,757 --> 00:01:55,858
BOB: Well that's great.&nbsp;

27
00:01:55,858 --> 00:02:03,237
(Q5) Now the trip I mentioned is just for a fortnight, but there might be the possibility of leading other tours after that.

28
00:02:03,237 --> 00:02:05,344
Would that fit in with your plans?

29
00:02:05,344 --> 00:02:07,201
MARGARET: That'd be fine. Margaret：

30
00:02:07,201 --> 00:02:09,285
[跟定位： five months原词重现， +同替 free=available] I'll be free for five months.

31
00:02:09,285 --> 00:02:17,795
[Q5答案句： May， 混了三个干扰项， 也都跟时间有关] My job is due to start on October the 2nd, and I'm available from May the 1st until late September.

32
00:02:17,795 --> 00:02:19,032
BOB: Good.&nbsp;

33
00:02:19,032 --> 00:02:22,259
(Q6) Now is there anything I need to know about the food you eat?

34
00:02:22,259 --> 00:02:31,118
We usually have one or two people in the group who don't eat meat, or have some sort of food allergy, so we're always very careful about that.

35
00:02:31,118 --> 00:02:33,818
[Q6答案句： 跟同替： allergic to = can't eat] MARGARET : Yes, I'm allergic to cheese.&nbsp;

36
00:02:33,818 --> 00:02:35,506
Would that be a problem?

37
00:02:35,506 --> 00:02:39,794
BOB: No, as long as we have enough notice, we can deal with that.&nbsp;

38
00:02:39,794 --> 00:02:41,879
MARGARET: That's great.&nbsp;

39
00:02:41,879 --> 00:02:47,273
(Q7) MARGARET : It sounds really interesting - would you like me to fill in an application form?&nbsp;

40
00:02:47,273 --> 00:02:49,078
BOB: Yes, please.&nbsp;

41
00:02:49,078 --> 00:02:50,965
Where should I post it to?

42
00:02:50,965 --> 00:03:03,835
[Q7答案句： 比较直观，跟上拼写即可] MARGARET:Could you send it to 27 Arbuthnot Place-A-R-B-U-T-H-N-0-T - Place, Dumfries .

43
00:03:03,835 --> 00:03:06,562
(Q8) BOB: And what's the postcode, please?&nbsp;

44
00:03:06,562 --> 00:03:10,533
[Q8答案句] MARGARET: DG7 4PH.&nbsp;

45
00:03:10,533 --> 00:03:14,101
[Q8干扰项： 正确答案+无关信息，] BOB: Was that P Papa or B Bravo?

46
00:03:14,101 --> 00:03:15,869
MARGARET: P Papa.&nbsp;

47
00:03:15,869 --> 00:03:16,873
BOB: Got that.&nbsp;

48
00:03:16,873 --> 00:03:23,741
(Q9) [定位词 interview， 听到预判时的答案词就要跟上，以防后面不再说了： Tuesday（Q9答案句）] If you could return the application form by Friday this week, we can interview you on Tuesday next week.

49
00:03:23,741 --> 00:03:25,830
[空前定位词： 2:30pm] Say half past two.

50
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:27,400
Would that be possible for you?

51
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,435
MARGARET: Yes, it's fine.&nbsp;

52
00:03:29,435 --> 00:03:33,675
[Q9干扰项：正确答案+无关信息] You're quite a long way from where I live, so I'll drive, over on Monday.

53
00:03:33,675 --> 00:03:36,104
(Q10) Should I bring anything to the interview?

54
00:03:36,104 --> 00:03:45,102
BOB: We'll have your application form, of course, but we'll need to see any certificates you've got that are relevant, in cycling, first aid, or whatever.&nbsp;

55
00:03:45,102 --> 00:03:46,559
MARGARET: OK.

56
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:56,418
[Q10答案句： prepare=plan， 锁定答案- talk] BOB: And at the interview we'd like to find out about your experience of being a tour guide.So could you prepare a ten-minute talk about that, please?&nbsp;

57
00:03:56,418 --> 00:04:01,846
You don't need slides or any complicated equipment - just some notes.

58
00:04:01,846 --> 00:04:05,579
MARGARET: Right. I'll start thinking about that straightaway!

59
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:07,508
BOB: Good.&nbsp;

60
00:04:07,508 --> 00:04:13,207
Well, we'll look forward to receiving your application form, and we'll contact you to confirm the interview.

61
00:04:13,207 --> 00:04:15,355
MARGARET: Thanks very much.&nbsp;

62
00:04:15,355 --> 00:04:16,727
BOB : Thank you, Margaret.&nbsp;

63
00:04:16,727 --> 00:04:19,227
Goodbye.

